:"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:animation","name":"topic:animation","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-01-09T17:34:10Z","updated_at":"2025-01-19T07:27:29Z","closed_at":"2025-01-15T08:01:23Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.2.x,  4.3.x and 4.4 dev 7\nLast worked as expected in 4.1.3\n\n### System information\n\nUbuntu 24.04, Windows 10\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf the audio clip of an AnimationPlayer is offset to the left  (to cover before 0 time range) then the sound clip will not play at all.  The engine will give the warning: _\"Found the key outside the animation range. Consider using the clean-up option in AnimationTrackEditor to fix it.\"_. This happens even if there is not actual key outside the animation range but the clip is just offset. \n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e1214e68-de01-4443-8117-39154e9d388f\n\nWhile we can clean up the animation, it does not have undo option so that making a fine tuning of the play time for a clip is a mess.\nIs this a feature? Godot 4.1 managed any audio clip offset without any problem.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate an animation player with an animation. Offset it to the left. The track will not play.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[audiobug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18365049/audiobug.zip)\n","closed_by":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.g